# What Prettier has no business reformatting.
#
# Without this, `prettier --check .` reports 109 files and is therefore read by
# nobody - the same failure mode as the missing `.prettierrc` it accompanies
# (enigma2_player-bxw). Everything below is either generated, owned by a tool,
# or checked by its own job.

# Build output.
dist/
site/dist/
site/.angular/
site/test-results/

# Generated: written by a script, so formatting it by hand is undone next run.
# `.mcp.json` says so in its own `$comment`: aiflow rewrites it from
# .aiflow/config.json, PowerShell-serialised, and a gate that fails on a file
# nobody edited is a gate that gets switched off.
TODO.md
.mcp.json
package-lock.json
site/package-lock.json

# Tool-owned. `.claude/agents/*.md` is the dangerous one: an agent whose YAML
# frontmatter stops parsing is dropped from the roster SILENTLY (AGENTS.md §5),
# and reflowing a description across lines is exactly how that happens.
.claude/
.aiflow/
.beads/
.agents/

# Prose, not code (enigma2_player-63s). Prettier's value in Markdown is
# cosmetic - list markers, table padding - and its cost here is not: AGENTS.md
# alone is 1723 changed lines, because every paragraph in this repository's
# rulebook is hand-wrapped and every table hand-aligned. Reflowing it would
# make `git blame` on the rules useless to settle an argument about them, and
# the same holds for the ADRs, the arc42 document and the READMEs. Line breaks
# in prose are an editorial decision, so they stay with the author.
#
# Code and configuration are the opposite case and are NOT excluded: there the
# formatter settles arguments instead of starting them.
*.md
